TriangularSets -- triangular decompositions of polynomial ideals
****************************************************************

Description
===========

This package allows to decompose polynomial ideals into *note triangular sets:
TriaSystem,
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..h, MonomialOrder=>Lex];                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal {a*d - b*c, c*f - d*e, e*h - f*g};                            |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : triangularize I                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = {{a*d - b*c, e, f} / d, {a*d - b*c, c*f - d*e, e*h - f*g} / {d, f, h},  |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     {c, d, e*h - f*g} / h, {c, d, e, f}, {a*d - b*c, c*f - d*e, g, h} / {d, |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     f}, {b, d, f, h}, {c, d, g, h}, {c, d, f, h}, {b, d, e, f}}             |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The method *note triangularize: triangularize, is implemented in M2 only for
monomial and binomial ideals. For the general case we interface to Maple.

This package also provides methods for manipulating triangular sets: 
  * *note dim(TriaSystem): dim_lpTriaSystem_rp, -- dimension of a triangular
    set
  * *note saturate(TriaSystem): saturate_lpTriaSystem_rp, -- saturated ideal of
    a triangular system
  * *note isRegularChain(TriaSystem): isRegularChain, -- whether a triangular
    set is a regular chain
  * *note isStronglyNormalized(TriaSystem): isStronglyNormalized, -- whether a
    triangular set is strongly normalized
  * *note RingElement % TriaSystem: RingElement % TriaSystem, --
    pseudo-remainder by a triangular set
  * resultant(RingElement,TriaSystem) (missing documentation)

References
==========

  * P. Aubry, D. Lazard, M. Moreno Maza (1999), "On the theories of triangular
    sets", in "Journal of Symbolic Computation", 28(1):105-–124
  * E. Hubert (2003), "Notes on triangular sets and triangulation-decomposition
    algorithms I: Polynomial systems", in "Springer"
  * M. Kalkbrener (1993), "A generalized Euclidean algorithm for computing
    triangular representations of algebraic varieties", in "Journal of Symbolic
    Computation", 15(2):143-–167
  * D. Lazard (1992), "Solving zero-dimensional algebraic systems", in "Journal
    of Symbolic Computation", 13(2):117-–131
  * D. Wang (2001), "Elimination methods", in "Springer Science & Business
    Media"

