degree(TriaSystem) -- product of the degrees in a triangular set
****************************************************************

  * Function: *note degree: (Macaulay2Doc)degree,
  * Usage: 
        degree T
  * Inputs:
      * T, an instance of the type *note TriaSystem: TriaSystem,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, product of the main degrees of the
        polynomials in T

Description
===========

This method returns the product of degrees of the polynomial in $T$ (the degree
in the *note main variables: mvar,). In the zero-dimensional case, this agrees
with degree of the *note saturated ideal: saturate_lpTriaSystem_rp, of $T$.

+----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a,b,c,d,e,f,g,h, MonomialOrder=>Lex];   |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = {a^2*d - b, c*f*h - d*e, e^3*h - f*g};     |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : T = triaSystem(R,F)                            |
|                                                    |
|       2                     3                      |
|o3 = {a d - b, c*f*h - d*e, e h - f*g} / {d, f*h, h}|
|                                                    |
|o3 : TriaSystem                                     |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : degree T                                       |
|                                                    |
|o4 = 6                                              |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : for f in F list degree(mvar f, f)              |
|                                                    |
|o5 = {2, 1, 3}                                      |
|                                                    |
|o5 : List                                           |
+----------------------------------------------------+


Caveat
======

It is assumed that the triangular set is a regular chain

See also
========

  * *note TriaSystem: TriaSystem, -- a triangular system
  * *note saturate(TriaSystem): saturate_lpTriaSystem_rp, -- saturated ideal of
    a triangular system

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note degree(TriaSystem): degree_lpTriaSystem_rp, -- product of the degrees
    in a triangular set
