initial -- initial of a polynomial
**********************************

  * Usage: 
        initial f
        initial(x,f)
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, 
  * Outputs:
      * h, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the initial of f

Description
===========

Returns the initial of a polynomial. The initial of a polynomial $f$ is the
leading coefficient of $f$ viewed as a univariate polynomial in its *note main
variable: mvar,.

+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x_0..x_3, MonomialOrder=>Lex];                |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : f = x_1^2*(x_2*x_3+2*x_3) + x_1*(x_2^2-1) + (x_2-x_3)|
|                                                          |
|      2         2        2                                |
|o2 = x x x  + 2x x  + x x  - x  + x  - x                  |
|      1 2 3     1 3    1 2    1    2    3                 |
|                                                          |
|o2 : R                                                    |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : initial f                                            |
|                                                          |
|o3 = x x  + 2x                                            |
|      2 3     3                                           |
|                                                          |
|o3 : R                                                    |
+----------------------------------------------------------+


