isPrimeSimple -- simple primality test of triangular systems
************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isPrimeSimple(T)
  * Inputs:
      * T, an instance of the type *note TriaSystem: TriaSystem,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, if the test is positive
        then sat(T) is prime; otherwise, it may or may not be prime

Description
===========

Let $T = (t_1,t_2,\cdots,t_k)$ be a triangular set (i.e., their *note main
variables: mvar, are distinct). This method verifies if the following
properties hold:

(i) the main degree of $t_i$ is one for $i=1,\dots,k-1$,

(ii) $t_k$ is an irreducible polynomial.

If these properties hold then the *note saturated ideal:
saturate_lpTriaSystem_rp, of $T$ is a prime ideal.

+--------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z,MonomialOrder=>Lex];|
+--------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = {x*y^2 - y*z, y^3 + z^2};    |
+--------------------------------------+
|i3 : T = triaSystem(R,F,{y});         |
+--------------------------------------+
|i4 : isPrimeSimple(T)                 |
|                                      |
|o4 = true                             |
+--------------------------------------+
|i5 : I = saturate T                   |
|                                      |
|                   2            2     |
|o5 = ideal (x*z + y , x*y - z, x  + y)|
|                                      |
|o5 : Ideal of R                       |
+--------------------------------------+
|i6 : isPrime I                        |
|                                      |
|o6 = true                             |
+--------------------------------------+


See also
========

  * *note TriaSystem: TriaSystem, -- a triangular system
  * *note saturate(TriaSystem): saturate_lpTriaSystem_rp, -- saturated ideal of
    a triangular system

