isRegularChain -- whether a triangular set is a regular chain
*************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isRegularChain(T)
  * Inputs:
      * T, an instance of the type *note TriaSystem: TriaSystem,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, true if T is a regular
        chain, and false otherwise

Description
===========

Let $T = (t_1,t_2,\cdots,t_k)$ be a triangular set (i.e., their *note main
variables: mvar, are distinct), and let $h$ be the product of its *note
initials: initial,. $T$ is a regular chain if the *note iterated resultant:
resultant_lpRingElement_cmTriaSystem_rp, is nonzero: $resultant(h,T)\neq 0$.

+--------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z,MonomialOrder=>Lex];|
+--------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = {x*y - y*z, y^2 - z^2};      |
+--------------------------------------+
|i3 : T = triaSystem(R,F,{y});         |
+--------------------------------------+
|i4 : isRegularChain(T)                |
|                                      |
|o4 = true                             |
+--------------------------------------+


See also
========

  * *note TriaSystem: TriaSystem, -- a triangular system
  * *note initial(TriaSystem): initial, -- initial of a polynomial
  * resultant(RingElement,TriaSystem) (missing documentation)

