isStronglyNormalized -- whether a triangular set is strongly normalized
***********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isStronglyNormalized(T)
  * Inputs:
      * T, an instance of the type *note TriaSystem: TriaSystem,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, true if T is strongly
        normalized, and false otherwise

Description
===========

Let $T = (t_1,t_2,\cdots,t_k)$ be a triangular set (i.e., their *note main
variables: mvar, are distinct). $T$ is strongly normalized if the *note
initial: initial, of each $t_i$ only involves *note free variables:
freeVariables,.

+----------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,t,s,MonomialOrder=>Lex];|
+----------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = {x + y^2 - t, t^2 -s};         |
+----------------------------------------+
|i3 : T = triaSystem(R,F,{});            |
+----------------------------------------+
|i4 : isStronglyNormalized(T)            |
|                                        |
|o4 = true                               |
+----------------------------------------+
+--------------------------------------+
|i5 : R = QQ[x,y,z,MonomialOrder=>Lex];|
+--------------------------------------+
|i6 : F = {x*y - y*z, y^2 - z^2};      |
+--------------------------------------+
|i7 : T = triaSystem(R,F,{y});         |
+--------------------------------------+
|i8 : isStronglyNormalized(T)          |
|                                      |
|o8 = false                            |
+--------------------------------------+


See also
========

  * *note TriaSystem: TriaSystem, -- a triangular system
  * *note initial(TriaSystem): initial, -- initial of a polynomial
  * *note freeVariables: freeVariables, -- free variables of a triangular set

