RingElement % TriaSystem -- pseudo-remainder by a triangular set
****************************************************************

  * Operator: *note %: (Macaulay2Doc)%,
  * Usage: 
        f % T
        pseudoRemainder(f,T)
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, 
      * T, an instance of the type *note TriaSystem: TriaSystem,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, pseudo-remainder of f
        by T

Description
===========

Returns the pseudo-remainder, $prem(f,T)$, of $f$ by a triangular set $T$.

Let $T = (t_1,t_2,\cdots,t_k)$ where $mvar(t_1)>\cdots>mvar(t_k)$. The
pseudo-remainder of $f$ by $T$ is $$prem(f,T) =
prem(\cdots(prem(prem(f,t_1),t_2)\cdots,t_k)$$

Remark:  If $T$ is a *note regular chain: isRegularChain,, then $f$ lies in its
*note saturated ideal: saturate_lpTriaSystem_rp, iff $prem(f,T)=0$.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a,b,c,d,e,f,g,h, MonomialOrder=>Lex];                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = {a*d - b*c, c*f - d*e, e*h - f*g};                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : H = {d, f, h};                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : T = triaSystem(R,F,H)                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = {a*d - b*c, c*f - d*e, e*h - f*g} / {d, f, h}                           |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : TriaSystem                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : (a*h - b*g) % T                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = 0                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : R                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : saturate T                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = ideal (e*h - f*g, c*h - d*g, c*f - d*e, a*h - b*g, a*f - b*e, a*d - b*c)|
|                                                                             |
|o6 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+


See also
========

  * pseudoRemainder(RingElement,RingElement,RingElement) (missing
    documentation)
  * *note saturate(TriaSystem): saturate_lpTriaSystem_rp, -- saturated ideal of
    a triangular system

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note RingElement % TriaSystem: RingElement % TriaSystem, --
    pseudo-remainder by a triangular set
