triangularize -- triangular decomposition of polynomial systems
***************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        triangularize(I)
        triangularize(R,F)
        triangularize(R,F,H)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, 
      * F, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of polynomials
      * H, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of polynomials
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note TriangularDecompAlgorithm: TriangularDecompAlgorithm, => ...,
        default value null, possible values: "Monomial", "Binomial", "Maple",
        "Epsilon"
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of triangular systems

Description
===========

Computes a triangular decomposition of a polynomial system. The package
implements algorithms for monomial and binomial sets. For arbitrary systems we
interface to Maple.

A polynomial system is a pair $(F,H)$, where $F\subset k[x]$ is a list of *note
equations: generators_lpTriaSystem_rp, and and $H\subset k[x]$ is a list of
*note inequations: ineqs,. The zero set of the system is $$Z(F/H) = \{x : f(x)=
0 for f\in F, h(x)\neq 0 for h\in H\}.$$ A triangular decomposition of $(F,H)$
is a collection of "simpler" polynomial systems $(T_1,U_1),\ldots,(T_r,U_r)$
such that $$Z(F/H) = Z(T_1/U_1)\cup\cdots\cup Z(T_r/U_r).$$ These simpler sets,
called *note triangular systems: TriaSystem,, have very nice algorithmic
properties.

As a first example we consider a case without inequations ($H=\emptyset$).

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..h, MonomialOrder=>Lex];                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = {a*d - b*c, c*f - d*e, e*h - f*g};                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : TT = triangularize(R,F,{})                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = {{a*d - b*c, e, f} / d, {a*d - b*c, c*f - d*e, e*h - f*g} / {d, f, h},  |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     {c, d, f, h}, {c, d, e*h - f*g} / h, {b, d, e, f}, {c, d, e, f}, {a*d - |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     b*c, c*f - d*e, g, h} / {d, f}, {b, d, f, h}, {c, d, g, h}}             |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : first TT                                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = {a*d - b*c, e, f} / d                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : TriaSystem                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

We now include some inequations.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : H = {b,d};                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : triangularize(R,F,H)                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = {{a*d - b*c, c*f - d*e, g, h} / {b, d, f}, {a*d - b*c, c*f - d*e, e*h - |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     f*g} / {b, d, f, h}, {a*d - b*c, e, f} / {b, d}}                        |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+


See also
========

  * *note TriaSystem: TriaSystem, -- a triangular system

