triangularizeBatch -- triangularize a batch of polynomial systems
*****************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        triangularizeBatch(alg,R,F,H)
  * Inputs:
      * alg, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, either "Maple" or "Epsilon"
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, 
      * F, a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, whose values are
        polynomial sets
      * H, a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, whose values are
        polynomial sets
  * Outputs:
      * a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, containing triangular
        decompositions of each system

Description
===========

Let $\{F_k: k\in K\}$ and $\{H_k: k\in K\}$ be collections of polynomial sets.
This function computes a triangular decomposition of each of the pairs
$(F_k,H_k)$.

Although *note triangularizeBatch: triangularizeBatch, is equivalent to calling
*note triangularize: triangularize, multiple times, the former is usually
faster since it avoids the cost of starting multiple Maple sessions.



