triaSystem -- a triangular system
*********************************

  * Usage: 
        triaSystem(R,F)
        triaSystem(R,F,H)
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, 
      * F, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of polynomials
      * H, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of polynomials (optional)
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note TriaSystem: TriaSystem,, given by the
        pair (F,H)

Description
===========

By default $H$ is chosen to be the set of *note initials: initial, of $F$.

+--------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a,b,c,d,e,f,g,h, MonomialOrder=>Lex]; |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = {a*d - b*c, c*f - d*e, e*h - f*g};       |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : H = {d, f, h};                               |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : triaSystem(R,F,H)                            |
|                                                  |
|o4 = {a*d - b*c, c*f - d*e, e*h - f*g} / {d, f, h}|
|                                                  |
|o4 : TriaSystem                                   |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : triaSystem(R,F)                              |
|                                                  |
|o5 = {a*d - b*c, c*f - d*e, e*h - f*g} / {d, f, h}|
|                                                  |
|o5 : TriaSystem                                   |
+--------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

It is not checked that $(F,H)$ is indeed a triangular system.

